{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>You redeemed Your people</b> — It is the pu'al, as though written: <b>You redeemed Your people</b> with an outstretched arm. The reason for mentioning Joseph with Jacob is that he sustained Israel, as written, <b>from there the Shepherd, the Stone of Israel</b>. And the meaning: for in the merit of Jacob and Joseph You redeemed their children. And like it, <b>also the seed of Jacob and David My servant I will not reject</b> — the meaning being, whoever is of noble sons; and the proof is that he said, <b>from their seed</b> they rule. And the one who says that Jacob stands in place of Aaron, does not speak correctly."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 77, :notes {0 "The heading 'גאלת עמך' cites the beginning of the verse; Ibn Ezra reads the qamatz form as pu'al. The clause 'מי שהוא מבני נדיבים' is rendered literally; the syntax of the surrounding sentence is compressed and the referent of 'the one who says' is unstated."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:34:53.384435215Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}